<title>JAPAN: Nintendo jumps on strong US sales of game software.</title>
<headline>Nintendo jumps on strong US sales of game software.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nintendo Co Ltd's shares jumped on Thursday morning, fuelled by robust sales of its new game software in the United States, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0126 GMT, the shares were up 410 yen at 9,710 on the</p>
<p>Osaka Securities Exchange.  </p>
<p>Retailers sold a record 300,000 copies of Nintendo's new Star Fox 64 video game in its first five days, executives of a U.S. unit of the video game maker said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>At a suggested retail price of $69.95 per copy, that represents an opening week &quot;box office&quot; take of nearly $21 million, the equivalent of a top Hollywood movie.</p>
</text>
